# Digital Marketing Strategy Document: Mahendras Online Growth Plan

## 📝 Introduction
Mahendra's Educational Private Limited is already a highly trusted brand for offline government exam coaching in India. However, to grow the online platform and compete with new-age edtech companies, a strong digital marketing plan is required.

This document outlines a complete digital marketing strategy to bring more traffic to the website, turn casual visitors into paying students, and build a massive online community. The plan focuses on four main pillars: 
* Search Engine Optimization (SEO)
* Social Media Marketing
* Paid Advertising
* Lead Nurturing

---

## 🔍 Part 1: Search Engine Optimization (SEO) Strategy
The website already gets good traffic from Google search, but this traffic must be multiplied and directed toward course conversion pages.

### 1. Target Keywords and Content Creation
* **High-Intent Keywords:** Informational articles must be created around keywords like *"best online coaching for SBI PO,"* *"SSC CGL live classes,"* and *"IBPS Clerk mock test pack."*
* **Daily Exam Updates:** The Update Hub must publish official exam notifications, syllabus changes, admit card download dates, and exam day guidelines within minutes of the official release to capture immediate search traffic.
* **Educational Material:** The site must continue publishing high-quality daily current affairs, vocabulary lists, and short math tricks.

### 2. On-Page SEO and Link Optimisation
* **Internal Linking:** Every free study blog must link directly to a related paid product page. For example, a blog post about banking English tips must contain text links to the *Premium Bank Video Course*.
* **Meta Descriptions and Titles:** All pages must use clear, catchy titles that show the current year (e.g., *"SBI PO Syllabus 2026: Download PDF Syllabus"*).
* **Image Optimization:** All blog images and banner graphics must use alt-text containing target keywords to rank well in Google Image Search.

---

## 📱 Part 2: Social Media Marketing Plan
Social media will be used to build trust, showcase top teachers, and share student success stories.

### 1. YouTube Strategy (The Primary Learning Channel)
* **Daily Free Live Sessions:** Faculty members will conduct daily 30-minute live classes solving previous year question papers for upcoming exams like SSC and Bank.
* **Shorts for Quick Tricks:** Short 60-second video clips will be uploaded daily to show quick math shortcuts, reasoning tricks, and vocabulary building.
* **Exam Analysis Videos:** Immediate live analysis sessions will be broadcasted on exam days as soon as students walk out of the exam halls to discuss difficulty levels and expected cut-off marks.

### 2. Instagram and Telegram Strategy (Community and Engagement)
* **Daily Quizzes on Instagram Stories:** Multiple-choice questions on general knowledge and current affairs will be posted daily to keep aspirants engaged.
* **Telegram Channel Distribution:** A dedicated Telegram channel will distribute daily free PDF notes, quiz links, and immediate batch announcements directly to students' mobile phones.
* **Student Success Reels:** Short video interviews of students who cleared their exams using Mahendras Online will be highlighted to provide strong social proof.

---

## 💳 Part 3: Paid Advertising and Remarketing Funnels
Paid ads will be used to bring immediate traffic to new online batches and bring back students who left the website without purchasing.

### 1. Google Search and Display Ads
* **Search Ads for Active Searchers:** Google Search Ads will target users who are actively searching for terms like *"buy bank test series online"* or *"join online coaching for SSC."*
* **Display Ads on Educational Sites:** Visual banner ads showcasing new batch start dates and discount offers will be displayed on popular educational news sites and job alert portals.

### 2. Meta and YouTube Remarketing Funnels
* **The Visit Tracker:** Tracking codes (pixels) will be placed on high-traffic pages like the Daily Current Affairs blog.
* **Targeted Ad Delivery:** Visitors who read the current affairs blog but do not buy a course will see specific ads on Facebook and Instagram within 24 hours. These ads will offer a 10% discount coupon code for the Daily Quiz Pack.
* **Video Retargeting on YouTube:** Users who watch free YouTube classes will be shown video ads promoting the structured, full-length live batches.

---

## 🎯 Part 4: Lead Nurturing and Conversion Tactics
Once a student shares their contact information via a free quiz or PDF download, regular communication will guide them toward buying a course.

### 1. WhatsApp and SMS Marketing
* **Immediate Welcome Message:** As soon as a student signs up, an automated WhatsApp message will deliver the promised free PDF study material along with a link to watch a demo class.
* **Weekly Exam Alerts:** Regular SMS updates will notify leads about upcoming application deadlines, followed by a recommendation to join the relevant preparation batch.
* **Flash Sale Notifications:** Short, urgent text messages will be sent during festival offers (e.g., *"Flat 50% off on all SSC Test Series — Valid only till midnight!"*).

### 2. Email Marketing Campaigns
* **The Educational Welcome Sequence:** A series of 5 automated emails will be sent over the first week, sharing free study tips, introducing top subject experts, and explaining the benefits of online learning.
* **Doubt-Solving Highlights:** Weekly emails will highlight how online students get their doubts cleared by teachers, addressing the biggest fear of online learners.

---

## 🗓️ Part 5: Implementation Timeline and Budget Allocation
The execution of this digital marketing strategy will follow a structured monthly setup and optimization plan.

### 1. 4-Week Launch Timeline
* **Week 1 (Setup and Tracking):** Install ad tracking codes on the website, set up automated WhatsApp tools, and plan the social media content calendar.
* **Week 2 (Content and Organic Launch):** Begin publishing SEO-optimized blogs, start daily Instagram quiz stories, and launch the Telegram PDF distribution channel.
* **Week 3 (Paid Campaign Activation):** Launch Google Search Ads and activate Meta remarketing ads for website visitors.
* **Week 4 (Review and Optimization):** Check which ads and keywords are bringing the most course sales, pause low-performing campaigns, and increase the budget for top-performing ads.

### 2. Budget Allocation Estimate
* 🎯 **40%** | Paid Retargeting Ads (Meta & YouTube)
* 🔍 **30%** | Google Search Ads (High-Intent Keywords)
* 📝 **20%** | Content Creation (Videos, PDFs, Blogs)
* ⚙️ **10%** | Automation Tools (WhatsApp & Email Software)
